<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central Provinces</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1861–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Central Provinces and Berar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Central Provinces was a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> formed in 1861 from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagar-madhya-pradesh">Saugor</a> and Nerbudda territories, with its capital at Nagpur. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berar">Berar</a> was joined to it in 1903, and from 1936 it was called the Central Provinces and Berar. Many small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a> were supervised from it, and in 1950 it became the Indian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>.</p></div>
